      "observed": "The input reverse-polarity stage uses T8, labeled AON6407, as a series high-side MOSFET. Its gate is fed from the input through R40 (33k) and clamped by D1 (12V) to GND. AON6407 is an N-channel MOSFET, and this arrangement does not provide the gate voltage above its source needed to turn it on as a high-side switch.",
      "expected": "The reverse-polarity stage should use a suitably driven high-side MOSFET arrangement, such as a P-channel MOSFET or an N-channel device with a proper gate driver, so the 24 V rail passes normally while reverse polarity is blocked.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Reverse polarity protection; T8 AON6407; R40 33k; D1 12V; page 1",
          "sheet and page": "Sheet /, page 1"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "README states the board has “reverse polarity protection”",
          "sheet and page": "Design specification, §2"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MOSFET is not properly enhanced in normal operation, so the board may receive power only through the MOSFET body diode or may fail to power up; the intended reverse-polarity protection is also not reliably achieved.",
      "confidence": 0.87
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["PR6", "H12"],
      "pins": ["PR6.1", "PR6.2", "PR6.3", "PR6.4", "H12.1", "H12.2", "H12.3", "H12.4"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "NET0081 (I2C_SDA)", "NET0030 (I2C_SCL)", "GND"],
      "observed": "The schematic shows PR6 labeled LiDAR connected through H12: its supply and ground are wired, and its SDA/SCL pins connect to the I2C bus.",
      "expected": "The specification says the TF-Luna LiDAR is not wired in this revision: its pins are free and it is excluded from the board.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "PR6 LiDAR; H12 pins connect to VCC, NET0081, NET0030 and GND; page 1",
          "sheet and page": "Sheet /, page 1"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "PR1 with on_board: no and all four pins typed free — it is not connected to any net",
          "sheet and page": "Design specification, §1"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The build adds a powered I2C LiDAR device that the specified design does not include, changing the sensor interface and potentially adding bus loading or device-address conflicts.",
      "confidence": 0.96
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is present: the high-side reverse-polarity stage uses an N-channel MOSFET without a suitable gate drive. The schematic also wires a LiDAR sensor that the specification says should be unconnected and excluded."
}

